===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The act or process of regaining something. 
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019| title=Regain Be Gone|author=Sameera Khan | page=| passage=Patients who plateau after weight loss are more likely to blame the '''regain''' on something that they are responsible for – the wrong course of action they took or a specic oversight that they kept repeating–rather than who they are.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021| title=Football in a Pandemic|author=Sam Hudson | page=| passage=By beginning deeper, this allows the opposition to start and build much higher, naturally luring them away from their own goal. As long as the actions after a '''regain''' are then quick, forward, and performed with quality, counter-attacks can prove a particularly useful attacking strategy to win football matches.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021| title=Superabsorbent Polymers|author=Sandra Van Vlierberghe, Arn Mignon | page=155| passage=The samples with SAPs showed a '''regain''' in strength when stored in an RH of more than 90%.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2022| title=Conservation of Architectural Heritage |author=Antonella Versaci, Hocine Bougdah, Natsuko Akagawa | page=375| passage=Negative collective memories are effective, as much as positive memories, in choosing a '''regain''' for lost heritage building associated with them. }}
# {{lb|en|textiles}} The amount of width a woven cloth grows by when the fibers swell, used to determine the width of the reed to use in weaving.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1912| title=Transactions of the National Association of Cotton Manufacturers|author=National Association of Cotton Manufacturers | page=105| passage=The number of ends per inch may vary to some slight extent at different places in the width of the cloth and in different pieces woven to the same particulars , but if the '''regain''' is correctly estimated , the calculated reed to be used will be the same, unless a special reed has been used in weaving the cloth.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008| title=Physical Properties of Textile Fibres |author=J. W. S. Hearle, W E Morton | page=190| passage=In particular, at high humidities the '''regain''' of wool is lower. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017| title=Wellington Sears Handbook of Industrial Textiles |author=Sabit Adanur | page=590| passage=Because of the fiber price per pound, and the size of the lots, the '''regain''' must be determined accurately.}}

